==English==
{{wikipedia|wear (disambiguation)|wear}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*wes-|id=dress}}
{{inh+|en|enm|weren}}, {{m|enm|werien}}, from {{inh|en|ang|werian||to clothe, cover over; put on, wear, use; stock (land)}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*waʀjan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wazjaną||to clothe}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wes-||to dress, put on (clothes)}}.

Cognate to {{cog|sa|वस्ते|tr=váste}}, {{cog|grc|ἕννυμι||put on}}, {{cog|la|vestis||garment}} ({{cog|en|vest}}), {{cog|sq|vesh||dress up, wear}}, {{cog|txb|wäs-}}, {{cog|xcl|զգենում}}, {{cog|cy|gwisgo}}, {{cog|hit|𒉿𒀸-|tr=waš-}}.

Originally a weak verb (i.e. with a past tense in -ed), it became irregular during the Middle English period by analogy with verbs like {{m|enm|beren}} (whence [[bear]]) and {{m|enm|teren}} (whence [[tear]]).

