===Etymology 2===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*wer-|id=heed}}
From {{inh|en|enm|weren}}, {{m|enm|werien}}, from {{inh|en|ang|werian||to guard, keep, defend; ward off, hinder, prevent, forbid; restrain; occupy, inhabit; dam up; discharge obligations on (land)}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*warjan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*warjaną||to defend, protect, ward off}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wer-||to close, cover, protect, save, defend}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|wer}}, {{m|sco|weir||to defend, protect}}, {{cog|nl|weren||to aver, ward off}}, {{cog|de|wehren||to fight}}, {{cog|sv|värja||to defend, ward off}}, {{cog|is|verja||to defend}}.

